WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:04.780
I think the fact that you did win an Oscar, Marlee,

2
00:00:04.780 --> 00:00:07.150
really did pave the way.

3
00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:10.850
One of the things that I have such a deep respect for

4
00:00:10.850 --> 00:00:15.850
is how the film treats the viewer

5
00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:19.190
as if they're just watching a family.

6
00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:20.410
Exactly.

7
00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:22.920
There are so many levels in this film.

8
00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:25.130 line:15%
It's not just for deaf people

9
00:00:25.130 --> 00:00:26.690 line:15%
or it's not about just deaf people.

10
00:00:26.690 --> 00:00:28.200 line:15%
It's for everyone.

11
00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.060 line:15%
And, and it does include deaf people.

12
00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:31.210 line:15%
It does include deaf culture.

13
00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:32.043 line:15%
It includes sign language,

14
00:00:32.043 --> 00:00:34.000 line:15%
but people who just happen to be deaf

15
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:34.940
it's sport of the story.

16
00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:36.350
We're human beings, just like anybody else.

17
00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:37.470
We're working class people.

18
00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:38.670
We earn living.

19
00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:39.780
We're trying to be parents.

20
00:00:39.780 --> 00:00:41.300
We're, you know, we have kids.

21
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.010
There are so many things that happen in this film

22
00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:45.170
that you'll recognize, that you can identify with.

23
00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:46.003
There's singing,

24
00:00:46.003 --> 00:00:46.836
there's deaf culture,

25
00:00:46.836 --> 00:00:47.669
there's fishing

26
00:00:47.669 --> 00:00:48.502
there's parenting,

27
00:00:48.502 --> 00:00:50.800
it's all in one package in this film.

28
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.610
And it's such a good film

29
00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:56.550
that people really love watching it from what I've seen.

30
00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:59.513
You know, again, going back to Hollywood,

31
00:01:00.680 --> 00:01:04.150
we're grateful for Vendôme and Pathé

32
00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:08.500
who put trust in our direction

33
00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:12.220
and put it in Sian Heder's hands as the director and writer

34
00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:14.923
to use authentic deaf actors, to tell this story.

35
00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:18.780
And for Apple TV+ to pick it up

36
00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:22.700
right after Sundance winning four awards,

37
00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:24.440
which is unprecedented

38
00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:27.860
for people to see and believe in us,

39
00:01:27.860 --> 00:01:30.180
really feels validating.

40
00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:33.740
It was a movie that everybody should see.

41
00:01:33.740 --> 00:01:34.580
It was a--

42
00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:35.890
And all the love that we got.

43
00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:38.240
It was a giant success at Sundance.

44
00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:42.153
It was bought for $25 million, an unprecedented amount.

45
00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:44.534
There you go, it's funny.

46
00:01:44.534 --> 00:01:46.401
(audience applauding)

47
00:01:46.401 --> 00:01:48.807
Thank you.

48
00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:51.470
I was looking at Sundance

49
00:01:51.470 --> 00:01:54.120
to see if anyone beat our record, not yet.

50
00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:57.760
You know, I don't need to brag, but I feel good.

51
00:01:57.760 --> 00:01:59.841
I've been waiting for someone to beat us.

52
00:01:59.841 --> 00:02:03.950
Well and just like Marlee mentioned,

53
00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:06.150
so our producers from Pathé and Vendôme,

54
00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:09.850
I feel like that group of folks planted a seed

55
00:02:09.850 --> 00:02:12.160 line:15%
and that seed blossomed

56
00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:16.820 line:15%
from this French film, which started to bloom

57
00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:18.560
and become stronger and stronger

58
00:02:18.560 --> 00:02:20.780
into a beautiful apple tree.

59
00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:23.290
A tree fell down, apple fell off that tree

60
00:02:23.290 --> 00:02:26.150
and down the hill like a snowball effect

61
00:02:26.150 --> 00:02:28.571
just plowing into Hollywood with deaf talent.

62
00:02:28.571 --> 00:02:31.571
(audience cheering)

63
00:02:33.948 --> 00:02:37.550
And for them, for the producers to hire us

64
00:02:37.550 --> 00:02:39.730
three actors who are deaf, authentic deaf,

65
00:02:39.730 --> 00:02:42.070
to carry a film, it's unprecedented, as I said

66
00:02:42.070 --> 00:02:43.210
it's never been done before.

67
00:02:43.210 --> 00:02:44.415
It is so rare.

68
00:02:44.415 --> 00:02:48.050
And your children are CODAs

69
00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:49.610
Four.
Four.

70
00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:50.620
And your daughter?

71
00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:52.670
I have a daughter, yes who is a CODA.

72
00:02:52.670 --> 00:02:54.280
Right now we have two interpreters here

73
00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:56.913
who actually CODAs themselves believe it or not.

74
00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:01.010
And so that's, my daughter's a CODA.

75
00:03:01.010 --> 00:03:02.223
Her daughter is a CODA.

76
00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:06.610
And so thank you for sharing this conversation

77
00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:09.010
and bridging two worlds between the hearing and deaf world.

78
00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:09.970
It's so important.

79
00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:11.710
And for so many CODAs who are younger

80
00:03:11.710 --> 00:03:13.260
who have hearing friends

81
00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:15.750
they really struggle to understand them.

82
00:03:15.750 --> 00:03:18.090
And that's why increasing this awareness

83
00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:18.923
with young people,

84
00:03:18.923 --> 00:03:20.275
they can become more accepting.

85
00:03:20.275 --> 00:03:22.858
(upbeat music)

